{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/pulls/5385","id":4518464130,"node_id":"PR_kwDOGiE5WM8AAAABDVJKgg","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5385","diff_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5385.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5385.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/5385","number":5385,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"refactor(request)!: derive body representations from the cached bytes","user":{"login":"yusukebe","id":10682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe","html_url":"https://github.com/yusukebe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`HonoRequest` caches each body representation (`json`, `text`, `formData`, ...) and converts between them when the body is read again in a different way. Every conversion loses something: the media type, the multipart boundary, or a rejected promise. #5129, #5365, and #5383 were each fixed by adding a special case to the conversion, and #5294 is the next one.\r\n\r\nThis PR removes the conversion itself, so this class of bugs cannot happen again, and the special cases go away. It keeps one source of truth and derives the other representations from it:\r\n\r\n- If the body is first read as `json()` or `text()`, the text is the source. Other representations are built from it.\r\n- Otherwise, the bytes from `arrayBuffer()` are the source.\r\n- `json()` caches its result, so it returns the same object every time.\r\n\r\nReading the same representation again returns the cache as before. Reading a different one no longer goes through a lossy conversion.\r\n\r\nRelated: #5129, #5365, #5383 (fixed individually in v4), #5294 (no longer needed with this change).\r\n\r\n### Performance\r\n\r\n`c.req.json()` is as fast as before. `benchmarks/fetch` (`body POST /json`) against `v5`: Bun 1.01x, Node 1.01x.\r\n\r\n### Behavior change\r\n\r\nWhen the bytes are rebuilt from the cached text, they can differ from the original (e.g., a BOM). In that case, `cloneRawRequest()` drops the `Content-Length` header and lets the runtime set it.\r\n\r\n### The author should do the following, if applicable\r\n\r\n- [x] Add tests\r\n- [x] Run tests\r\n- [x] `bun run format:fix && bun run lint:fix` to format the code\r\n- [ ] Add [TSDoc](https://tsdoc.org/)/[JSDoc](https://jsdoc.app/about-getting-started) to document the code\r\n","created_at":"2026-09-13T11:30:31Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T07:27:45Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"f50a1e29de87dfb7a4cd64fbcb2b6efe40067617","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":7070693471,"node_id":"LA_kwDOGiE5WM8AAAABpXI4Xw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/labels/v5","name":"v5","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/pulls/5385/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/pulls/5385/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/5385/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com